---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title='Barbershop Websites in Las Vegas and Henderson | NV Labs'
  description='A free demo website for your Las Vegas or Henderson barbershop with booking, barber pages, and hours. Call or text (501) 413-3386.'
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Las Vegas and Henderson barbershops</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">A barbershop website for Las Vegas and Henderson shops</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Booking, barber pages, hours, and walk-in policy clear up top. Call or text
        to get started.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="walkin-title">
      <h2 id="walkin-title">Walk in or book? Tell them up front</h2>
      <p>
        The most common question a barbershop gets is "Do you take walk-ins?" Your site should
        answer it the second someone lands on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whether you're walk-ins only, appointments only, or a mix, I'll make it clear at the top. If
        walk-ins are slower on weekday mornings, we can say that too.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="book-title">
      <h2 id="book-title">Your booking link, easy to find</h2>
      <p>
        If you already use a booking app, great. I'll put a big "Book Now" button right where people
        expect it, and on every barber's page. No hunting through menus. If you don't use one yet, a
        "Call or Text to Book" button works just as well.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="barber-title">
      <h2 id="barber-title">A page for every barber</h2>
      <p>People don't just pick a shop. They pick a barber. I'll give each barber their own section with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Their name and photo</li>
        <li>What they're known for (fades, beard work, designs, kids' cuts)</li>
        <li>The days they work</li>
        <li>Their personal booking link or Instagram</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That way a customer who loved their cut last time can find the same chair again.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="svc-title">
      <h2 id="svc-title">Services and hours, no guessing</h2>
      <p>
        I'll lay out your services in a clean list: cuts, fades, lineups, beard trims, hot towel
        shaves, kids' cuts, and anything else you offer. Your hours go right next to it, with notes
        like late nights on Fridays or closed Sundays.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="local-title">
      <h2 id="local-title">Local to the Valley</h2>
      <p>
        I'm based in Las Vegas, so I know the area. Whether your shop is in Henderson near Green
        Valley, out in Summerlin, in Spring Valley, or over in North Las Vegas, I'll write your site
        so people nearby can find you when they search "barbershop near me."
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="see-title">
      <h2 id="see-title">See it before you commit</h2>
      <p>
        I'll build a free demo of your shop's site and send you the link. If you and your barbers
        like it, I put it live. If not, no problem at all. We work by call and text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>Can each barber have their own booking link?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. If each barber books through their own account, I'll link each one from their own
            section.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>We're mostly walk-ins. Do we still need a website?</h3>
          <p>
            A site helps people know you exist, see your hours, and check out your work before they
            walk in. For a walk-in shop, that's often the difference between someone showing up or
            going somewhere else.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>How do we review the demo?</h3>
          <p>
            I text or call you with the link. You and your barbers can open it on your phones and
            tell me what to change.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's build your shop's demo</h2>
      <p>Send me your shop name and I'll get started.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
